        "execSummary":  "This architecture solves one of the most common enterprise blockers for deploying AI agents at scale: how to give an agent access to data across organizational silos without creating a centralized data lake or bypassing existing access controls. Using MCP as the integration layer with Cedar for authorization means enterprises can extend existing identity governance to agent interactions — a critical requirement for audit and compliance. For customer support and operations leaders, this pattern enables agents that can traverse account data, knowledge bases, and ticketing systems while respecting data residency and role-based permissions. The AWS-native dependency (AgentCore, Bedrock, Cedar) means organizations on other clouds will need to adapt the pattern.",
